  "shared_assessment_notes": [
    "The shared theorem applies to an already total Nat-indexed scalar function over an Archimedean linearly ordered commutative ring. Only rho<1, an eventual child-sum bound and an eventual upper recurrence are assumed. Function/toll values may be signed; neither function nor child-map monotonicity is required. It does not prove termination of an independently proposed recursive definition.",
    "The proof selects an enlarged finite prefix using an Archimedean natural multiple, takes a genuine finite maximum of its actual values, then chooses a nonnegative slope before the universally quantified input. Natural child nonnegativity and the contracting sum establish both strict child decreases. Explicit toll absorption, including signed toll coefficients, closes strong induction.",
    "The quarter recurrence is independently well-founded at its own cutoff1 and clients establish the actual values1,1,5,7,19,31 at0,1,2,4,8,16 before applying the shared scalar bound. The signed Int client exercises a carrier without a field instance and a negative toll. Negative-square and parameterwise counterclients prevent inference of norm bounds or exchange of parameter and constant quantifiers.",
    "All21 full emitted types independently agree with the assessed source, including the exact ordered-ring/Archimedean classes, arbitrary signed coefficients, lack of monotonicity/sign premises and exists-constants-before-input order.",
    "The accepted shared documentation explicitly preserves the distinction between this division-free affine existence theorem and the chapter-specific sharp rounded-ceiling constants, actual algorithm termination and cost correspondence. It dates historical preparation status and directs current acceptance to preserved control evidence. The Q-to-XR entrypoint/map change has been read; remaining complete Chapter3 map composition still requires review."
  ],
